{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe three provider overlays contain repeated or historical comments identified by the audit and revalidated on current `origin/main`. Shortening them must preserve provider-selection and credential isolation contracts.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only standalone comments and blank lines in the declared TOML files. Preserve configuration values byte-for-byte and retain the minimum current rationale needed by external-test operators.\n\n## Scope\n- `anthropic.toml` — Preserve explicit config-file-path coverage, credential name, provider-qualified `[llm] model`, and all three model-class slots so ambient provider defaults cannot leak in.\n- `bedrock.toml` — Preserve inference-profile-only IDs with nonuniform suffixes; verbatim discovery from `aws bedrock list-inference-profiles`; region and ambient-AWS credentials; provider-qualified scalar model plus all class slots; and matrix-only Anthropic-key blanking.\n- `openai.toml` — Preserve best-effort support tier, credential, verified models, provider-qualified scalar model, and all class slots.\n\nConsumers are the config loader, external provider matrix, current `rebar.toml` model/region defaults, Compose, and provider-pin tests. The stale `external-integration.yml` comment that mentions only model classes is owned by `sphalerite-bereft-tortoise`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only standalone comments or blank lines in the three declared overlays.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer contract has a PASS row with concrete before/after citations in a leaf-linked session log authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited comment block has an independent `bloat-removal` PASS row confirming that redundant, obvious, duplicated, or historical prose was removed while current non-obvious rationale remained.\n- [ ] Focused provider/config tests, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and repository lint pass; no missing or FAIL semantic-preservation row remains.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded comment-only guard, provider-matrix tests, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv lint."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788602389232914001,"uuid":"7639e83e-7088-4d16-a321-1bf44cfdb130"}